  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ It is used for troubleshooting, analysis, development and education.\n \n == What’s New\n \n-NOTE: This is the last release branch with support for 32-bit Windows.\n+__This is the last release branch with support for 32-bit Windows.__\n Updates will no longer be available after May 22, 2024 for that platform.\n wsbuglink:17779[]\n \n@@ -31,15 +31,28 @@ wsbuglink:17779[]\n \n // The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-// * wssalink:2022-07[]\n-// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n-// wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n+* wssalink:2022-07[]\n+OPUS dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:18378[].\n // cveidlink:2022-xxxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: xxxxx\n-// Fixed in release-3.6: xxxxx\n-// Fixed in release-3.4: xxxxx\n+// Fixed in master: 749a8d0912\n+// Fixed in release-4.0: 0e1a66eced\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 5db46d3a7c\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n-// CWE-???\n+// CWE-120\n+// * Stack Overflow Write - OPUS dissector - dissect_opus() frames wsbuglink:18378[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2022-08[]\n+USB-HID dissector crash on Windows.\n+wsbuglink:18384[].\n+// cveidlink:2022-xxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: 402bb0ee81\n+// Fixed in release-4.0: f79c81f5d5\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 025ba5fdf6\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-134: Use of Externally-Controlled Format String\n+// * Crash in USB-HID dissector on Windows wsbuglink:18384[].\n+\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -48,6 +61,21 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark keeps banging out random chords on your piano and yelling “LIPS LIKE SUGUAR, SUGAR KISSES” because it was funny that one time at a party.\n \n+* Wireshark no longer calculates Statistics -> Service Response Time -> FC properly. wsbuglink:16084[].\n+\n+* Qt: Crash when opening Statistics -> Service Response Time -> DCE-RPC. wsbuglink:18319[].\n+\n+* Qt: Crash when closing 3 of the 14 dialogs available from the menu item Statistics -> 29West wsbuglink:18334[].\n+\n+* TCP: Dissector bug, protocol TCP, in packet 13: .../wireshark/epan/reassemble.c:1420: failed assertion \"tvb_bytes_exist(tvb, offset, frag_data_len)\" wsbuglink:18335[].\n+\n+* Packet diagram field values are not terminated wsbuglink:18428[].\n+\n+* Decoding bug H.245 userInput Signal wsbuglink:18468[].\n+\n+* CFDP dissector doesn't handle \"destination filename\" only wsbuglink:18495[].\n+\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n@@ -61,18 +89,35 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.4.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n+// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.6.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+ASN.1 PER\n+BGP\n+CFDP\n+FC\n+GSMTAP\n+GTP\n+HTTP\n+IEEE 802.11\n+IPv4\n+ISAKMP\n+NAS-5GS\n+OPUS\n+PFCP\n+RTPS\n+TCP\n+USB HID\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// [commaize]\n-// --\n-// --\n+[commaize]\n+--\n+BLF\n+--\n \n === New File Format Decoding Support\n \n",
